"""
All NSE — the main scanner's view, over every listed stock.

Goes in /opt/breakoutscanner-lab/pages/6_All_NSE.py

WHAT THIS IS
------------
The same cards and metric tiles as the main `app` page, reading the nightly
snapshot instead of scanning live.

The main page calls scan_universe(), which fetches bars per symbol. Over 3,303
symbols that is roughly half an hour in a browser session, and Streamlit would
drop the connection first. The snapshot has already done that work overnight,
so the same view over the whole market returns in milliseconds.

The trade-off, stated plainly: this shows the last completed session, not an
intraday scan. For "what broke out", that is the right frame anyway — a
breakout is confirmed on a close, and a stock above its level at 2pm that
closes below it did not break out.

STYLING
-------
CSS copied verbatim from app.py. Not imported, because app.py is a Streamlit
script and importing it would execute the entire main page as a side effect.
Streamlit injects CSS per page regardless, so each page needs its own copy.

ONE RULE THE MAIN PAGE DOES NOT HAVE
------------------------------------
`traded_today`. Every snapshot row is stamped with the build date, but 326 of
3,046 stocks did not print a bar that day — illiquid names do not trade every
session. Without that filter, a stock that broke out two days ago and has been
silent since appears under "today". The toggle below lets you see them, off by
default.
"""

